# x-release-please-start-version
PRINT
    Inux v1.0.0 — Vinod Liyanage

    | Command | Purpose |
    |---|---|
    | `/inux help` | Show commands. |
    | `/inux setup` | Set up tools and sign in. |
    | `/inux task <id>` | Load a Jira ticket and create task files. |
    | `/inux branch create` | Create and switch to a local task branch. |
    | `/inux commit changes` | Stage intended changes and create a local commit. |
    | `/inux estimate [request]` | Draft, improve, explain, or publish an estimate. |
    | `/inux ts [request]` | Generate, improve, or publish a standalone technical summary. |
    | `/inux technical summary [request]` | Alias for `/inux ts [request]`. |
    | `/inux pr [request]` | Prepare, refine, explain, or publish a PR. |

    Replace `[request]` with what you want the agent to do. A request is required.
    The agent selects the matching route from plain language. If the request is missing,
    unsupported, conflicting, or ambiguous, it shows a usage error and stops.

    Examples: `/inux estimate improve the reasons`, `/inux ts summarize these changes`,
    `/inux pr improve the title`.

    Publishing requires an explicit `/inux estimate publish`,
    `/inux ts publish` (or `/inux technical summary publish`), or `/inux pr publish` request.

# x-release-please-end
